{"totalPapers":99,"techniqueGroups":[{"id":"spaced-repetition","name":"Spaced Repetition","icon":"📅","description":"Reviewing material at increasing intervals strengthens long-term retention by leveraging the spacing effect.","practiceTip":"This system uses SM-2 scheduling to optimize your review intervals based on mastery.","papers":[{"title":"Memory: A Contribution to Experimental Psychology","authors":["Ebbinghaus H"],"year":1885,"evidenceLevel":"foundational_theory","relevanceScore":90,"keyFindings":["Discovered the forgetting curve — exponential decay of memory over time","Demonstrated that spaced repetition dramatically slows forgetting","Established the savings method for measuring memory retention"]},{"title":"Distributed practice in verbal recall tasks: A review and quantitative synthesis","authors":["Cepeda NJ","Pashler H"],"year":2006,"evidenceLevel":"meta_analysis","relevanceScore":98,"keyFindings":["Distributed practice significantly improves long-term retention","Optimal inter-study intervals depend on retention interval","Spacing effects are robust across diverse verbal recall tasks"]},{"title":"The right time to learn: Mechanisms and optimization of spaced learning","authors":["Smolen P","Zhang Y"],"year":2016,"evidenceLevel":"review","relevanceScore":95,"keyFindings":["Spaced learning engages synaptic tagging and capture mechanisms","Optimal spacing intervals can be computationally modeled","Molecular mechanisms of spacing effect identified"]},{"title":"Spacing Repetitions Over Long Timescales: A Review and a Reconsolidation Explanation","authors":["Toppino TC","Gerbier E"],"year":2014,"evidenceLevel":"review","relevanceScore":95,"keyFindings":["Spacing effects persist over long timescales","Memory reconsolidation provides mechanistic explanation","Expanding schedules may optimize long-term retention"]},{"title":"Using spacing to enhance diverse forms of learning: Review and implications for instruction","authors":["Carpenter SK","Cepeda NJ"],"year"