leep for best consolidation. Even a 20-minute nap after study boosts retention.","papers":[{"title":"The memory function of sleep","authors":["Rasch B","Born J"],"year":2013,"evidenceLevel":"review","relevanceScore":98,"keyFindings":["Active systems consolidation during sleep transforms memories","Sleep spindles and slow oscillations coordinate memory transfer","Sleep selectively strengthens relevant memories"]},{"title":"About sleep's role in memory","authors":["Diekelmann S","Born J"],"year":2010,"evidenceLevel":"review","relevanceScore":98,"keyFindings":["Sleep actively consolidates memories through replay mechanisms","Both NREM and REM sleep contribute to different memory types","Sleep-dependent consolidation enhances both declarative and procedural memory"]},{"title":"Sleep, learning, and memory at a glance","authors":["Abel T","Havekes R"],"year":2013,"evidenceLevel":"review","relevanceScore":95,"keyFindings":["Sleep is essential for memory encoding, consolidation, and retrieval","Sleep deprivation impairs hippocampal function","Molecular mechanisms of sleep-dependent memory identified"]},{"title":"Sleep deprivation and memory: Meta-analytic reviews","authors":["Newbury CR","Monaghan P"],"year":2022,"evidenceLevel":"meta_analysis","relevanceScore":95,"keyFindings":["Sleep deprivation before learning impairs encoding","Sleep deprivation after learning impairs consolidation","Both effects are robust across study types"]},{"title":"Sleep and memory consolidation in healthy, neurotypical children, and adults","authors":["Webb AR"],"year":2024,"evidenceLevel":"systematic_review","relevanceScore":92,"keyFindings":["Sleep consolidation benefits confirmed across age groups","Slow-wave sleep particularly important for declarative memory","Consistent benefits for both children and adults"]},{"title":"Promoting memory consolidation during sleep: A meta-analysis of targeted memory reactivation","authors":["Hu X","Cheng LY"],"year":2020,"evidenceLevel":"meta_analysis","rel